  "notes": "Built from bulletin scraper for 2023-2024 catalog year. Like 2022, this plan did not include MATH 3/4/21/22 or CHEM 202, which are prerequisites for CHEM 110 and VBSC 438 respectively. These were added in the 2026 plan. QUALITY-AUDIT FIX #1: self-verification (build_full_plan) showed 10 courses permanently unschedulable (CHEM 110/111/112/113/210/212/213, BIOL 240W, VBSC 230, BMB 211) from the missing real CHEM 110 prereq chain (MATH 22 <- MATH 21 <- MATH 4 <- MATH 3; MATH 140/141 don't substitute), identical to PHTX-2022's own gap and already fixed in PHTX-2026.json. Added MATH 3 (Semester 1), MATH 4 (Semester 2), MATH 21 (Semester 3), MATH 22 + CHEM 202 (Semester 4), matching PHTX-2026.json's fix verbatim. QUALITY-AUDIT FIX #2: raw-HTML inspection of the archived 2023-24 bulletin page (same table structure as 2022-23) shows 'VBSC 438 (or Elective or 400-level Supporing Course)' is a single real requirement printed as an alternative-placement row in BOTH Semester 6 and Semester 8 -- this file had modeled it as a hard-required course in both, double-counting a single 3cr requirement. Converted the Semester 6 occurrence to a generic elective/support-course slot, keeping Semester 8's as the real requirement (matching PHTX-2024/2025's own correct single-occurrence treatment). The same real double-placement structure applies to 'VBSC 395/496' (one flexible 2-3cr requirement the bulletin prints across up to 4 terms) -- this file had it hard-required in both Semester 7 and Semester 8; converted the Semester 8 occurrence to a generic slot, keeping Semester 7's, matching PHTX-2026.json's own collapse of this exact quirk. QUALITY-AUDIT FIX #3: fixing the MATH/CHEM chain exposed VBSC 451's own real prereq (BMB 251 or MICRB 201, per vbsc_catalog.json) was never in this plan (VBSC 451 was dropped from the curriculum by 2026, so this gap never surfaced there). BMB 251's own prereq is just CHEM 112 (already scheduled Semester 2). Added BMB 251 (Semester 5). Re-verified with build_full_plan(start_year=2023, today=2023-07-01): 0 'Could not schedule' warnings (previously 10), 142 scheduled credits (matches PHTX-2026.json's own 142). QUALITY-AUDIT FIX (VBSC cross-listing): 'VBSC/ERM 431' and 'VBSC/BMB 433' were modeled as fully generic slots because bulletin_scraper.py's _extract_linked_codes only recognizes single-code <a> anchor text and doesn't parse this bulletin's real slash-combined anchor format (e.g. a single <a href=\"/search/?P=VBSC 431\" title=\"VBSC/ERM 431\">VBSC/ERM 431</a> tag) -- confirmed via raw-HTML inspection that both are real, linked, catalog-verified courses (VBSC 431, VBSC 433), and already modeled as such in PHTX-2026.json. Converted both to specific 'course' items matching 2026's treatment.",
